  "channelFailureKindUnknown": "unclassified",
  "channelFailureHelpTitle": "How to read the last failure",
  "channelFailureHelpBody": "This line is evidence only, not a current verdict: it remains even after the channel recovers.\n\nNetwork unreachable — the request never reached the other side (no connection, DNS failure, or timeout).\nServer returned an error — the other side returned 4xx or 5xx; the exact status code is in the delivery log.\nRate limited — the platform requested a lower sending rate (429); the system waits and retries automatically.\nRejected by the platform — HTTP succeeded, but the platform judged the content non-compliant (non-zero errcode); retrying will not help.\nStopped on this device — the message was stopped here before sending (push paused or engine not running).\nUnclassified — an HTTP status code exists, but it is 2xx or 3xx with no sign of a business rejection; the system does not guess.\n\nN in a row — the number of consecutive failures ending at this one; a success in between resets the count.",
