  "privacyTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyWelcome": "Welcome to NoticeTransmit!",
  "privacyBody": "• Notification content is matched and filtered on-device, and forwarded only to the Webhook, email address, or Fnthink device you configure\n• Fnthink Push messages are relayed through the server you choose; if you never use Fnthink Push, notification content never leaves this device\n• Push history is AES-256 encrypted and stored in a local database\n• Channel credentials (Webhook/email) are encrypted with AndroidKeyStore\n• Crash reporting (Tencent Bugly) is off by default; it only collects necessary crash logs for fixing issues after you enable it in settings, and no personal information is collected\n• Photo capture (off by default): after you enable \"Camera\" on this device and grant the camera permission, a paired device may ask this device to take a photo; the photo file stays on this device, and the image is relayed with the reply message through the server you choose and stored in both sides' message history",
