  "fnthinkSettingsTitle": "Fnthink push settings",
  "fnthinkReceive": "Receive pushes",
  "fnthinkReceiveDesc": "Messages are fetched from the server only while this is on; when it is off, neither sending nor receiving occurs.",
  "fnthinkChannelDisclosure": "Whether an incoming push sounds, vibrates, or displays a banner is determined by the \"Fnthink Push · Inbox\" notification channel in system notification settings. This device creates the channel at the top tier: importance = urgent (heads-up banner), sound = system default notification tone, vibration = on. Some vendor systems (e.g. Xiaomi) provide additional per-app floating-window and lock-screen switches above this layer; these must be checked in system settings.",
  "fnthinkOpenChannelSettings": "Open system channel settings",
  "fnthinkConsentTitle": "Allow notification content to be relayed through the server?",
  "fnthinkConsentMsg": "① Not using push: everything runs on this device; notification content never touches a server.\n② Only forwarding notifications locally: same — the server collects no notification content at all.\n③ Using push: messages must be relayed through the server to reach this phone. Until delivered, the body is encrypted and stored on the server for at most 7 days and is deleted immediately on delivery or expiry; pairing codes and the identity private key are never uploaded, and audits keep metadata only (no bodies).",
  "fnthinkConsentAgree": "I understand and agree",
  "fnthinkConsentGranted": "Content relay through the server is allowed",
  "fnthinkConsentPending": "Relay consent has not been granted; all server-relayed sending and receiving are stopped.",
  "fnthinkConsentNotGranted": "This device has not consented to relaying content through the server; this action was not performed.",
  "fnthinkRelayConsentSection": "Relay through the server",
  "fnthinkConsentRevoke": "Revoke consent",
  "fnthinkConsentRevokeTitle": "Revoke consent to relaying through the server?",
  "fnthinkConsentRevokeMsg": "After revoking, the following stop working immediately: server-relayed messaging (the next poll cycle of the receive loop will stop), remote control, endpoint create/update/delete, pair initiation and approval, fnthink channel create/enable/send, and text-bearing tests. Non-intrusive probes are unaffected (they only read capability levels, never trigger delivery). Pair lists, endpoints, channel configs, message history and pair records will not be deleted. Re-enabling requires going through the consent flow again",
  "fnthinkConsentRevokeDone": "Revoked: server-relayed sending and receiving, and remote control, are unavailable. No configuration or history was deleted.",
  "fnthinkConsentGateTitle": "This operation requires routing content through the server first",
  "fnthinkConsentGateMsg": "\"{action}\" requires the \"content relayed through the server\" consent first: fnthink messaging, endpoint management, pairing and channel delivery all route through the relay server. Please review and consent on the \"Fnthink → Receive Push\" page first (full text is available before consent). Return here after consenting and tap again to continue.",
